ul.li:
token contents are encrypted and authenticated rather
          than encoded in cleartext or with reversible obfuscation
          ();

each token is bound to one issuing tenant and one
          destination registrable domain, and is accepted at most once
          ();

dl.dd:
The server-side record of consumed token identifiers used
        to enforce single use ( and
        ).

section.t:
Browser-stored identity data is encoded and tamper-evident;
it is not encrypted. Cross-domain tokens are encrypted and
signed. Consent state is stored as plain values.

ol.li:
16 octets (128 bits) from a cryptographically secure
          random source  (in browsers,
          crypto.getRandomValues
          );

Envelope completeness and limits: tid,
          dst, iv, ct nonempty strings
          within the limits of ;
          decoded IV exactly 12 octets, decoded tag exactly 16
          octets, decoded ciphertext between 1 and 8192 octets;
          otherwise MALFORMED_TOKEN.

Issue-time check: iat is a number no further
          than 60 seconds in the future (clock-skew allowance);
          otherwise INVALID_IAT.

tr.td:
The signed source or destination domain is not
            currently authorized for the token's tenant (also
            returned at issuance;
            ).

A grant request's Origin header disagrees
            with the requested domain (grant issuance,
            ).

ul.li:
Uses a durable shared replay store in production;
          refuses to start without one
          ().

DNS authorization published and revalidated;
          authenticated management endpoints
          (,
